    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d651">

                <pb facs="0556" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.415 C35/45.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The French Ambassador to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">French Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 6, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: A delegation presided
                    over by Monsieur Hanotaux, member of the French Academy, former Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs, and composed of some twenty persons, will soon arrive in
                    America to offer to the Champlain Committee a bust by Rodin with which to
                    ornament the monument now building at Crown Point.</p>
                <p>This delegation, which comprises several members of the French Academy, two
                    Generals, a Senator, the President of the Academy of Fine Arts, several members
                    of the Institut, etc., will come to New York on board the S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">La France</hi> arriving about the 26th instant.</p>
                <p>I should be very grateful to your excellency if you would request the competent
                    authorities to expedite the landing and examination <pb facs="0557" n="441"
                        xml:id="pg441"/> of the baggage of the delegation as much as compatible with
                    the regulations.</p>
                <p>The stay of the delegation in the United States must be very brief, as they
                    expect to depart after about ten days.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.].</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jusserand</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
